Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: check the hcd before reading a port's speed

dwc3_qcom_read_usb2_speed() takes the hcd from the drvdata of dwc->xhci
and reads hcd->self.root_hub.  dwc->xhci is the xhci-hcd platform device
that dwc3 creates in host role.  It stays registered when the xhci-plat
probe fails, and its drvdata is NULL then.  dwc3_qcom_suspend() reads
the port speeds in host role whenever wakeup is set, and a runtime
suspend always sets it.

Seen on an SM-X710 on 2026-11-21.  After a boot with a hub attached, a
later attach in host role registered a new xHCI, and its probe failed
("xhci-hcd xhci-hcd.2.auto: Host halt failed, -110", then "can't setup:
-110" and "probe with driver xhci-hcd failed with error -110").  6.6 s
later the controller runtime-suspended (user space allows runtime PM
for it), and the glue oopsed on the pm workqueue: a NULL
pointer dereference at virtual address 0x58, pc
dwc3_qcom_suspend+0x118/0x264, called from
dwc3_qcom_runtime_suspend+0x44/0x60.  The faulting load is
hcd->self.root_hub, at offset 0x58 in that build, from the NULL drvdata.

The pm worker died with the controller's runtime PM status at
"suspending".  At the next reboot the stop job of
ubuntu-gts9u-usb-runtime-pm.service, a shell writing the controller's
power/control, blocked behind that status and could not be killed:
shutdown stalled for 7.5 minutes in user space.

A system suspend reads the speeds as well when the glue may wake the
system, which the gts9 family overlay sets up (wakeup-source on
usb@a600000), unless the controller is runtime-suspended already.

Return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN when there is no hcd.  The glue then arms its
wakeup interrupts as for an empty port, and the suspend completes.

This does not fix the failed probe.  That is the controller context lost
while the USB GDSCs were off, which gcc-sm8550-usb-gdscs-retention.patch
addresses.  The xhci-hcd device stays without a driver until the next
role change replaces it.  dwc3-qcom-legacy.c has the same code; the
SM8550 boards use the flattened binding, and it is left alone.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -240,6 +240,13 @@ static enum usb_device_speed dwc3_qcom_r
 	 */
 	hcd = platform_get_drvdata(dwc->xhci);
 
+	/*
+	 * With no xHCI driver bound to dwc->xhci, as after a failed probe,
+	 * there is no hcd and no root hub to read the speed from.
+	 */
+	if (!hcd)
+		return USB_SPEED_UNKNOWN;
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB
 	udev = usb_hub_find_child(hcd->self.root_hub, port_index + 1);
 #else
